\ mandelbrot, matrix — vectorized variant of pyperformance/mandelbrot.h2o.
\ Every pixel's z is iterated at once as an N x N matrix: element-wise *, +, -,
\ and a > mask replace the scalar per-pixel loop, so the matrix kernels' SIMD
\ does the work. There is no per-pixel early exit — all max-iter iterations run
\ for every pixel and `escaped` accumulates the escape mask; a pixel is in-set
\ iff it never escaped (escaped = 0), giving the same count as the serial version.
\ CR[y,x] = 2x/N - 1.5 and CI[y,x] = 2y/N - 1 are built as rank-1 outer products.

1000 constant n
50 constant max-iter

variable c-real  variable c-imag  variable zr  variable zi  variable escaped

: setup
  | ones-col ones-row cr-row ci-col |
  1.0 n array-of vector to ones-col
  1.0 n array-of 1 n matrix to ones-row
  0.0 n 1.0 f- 1.0 matrix-range 2.0 * n / 1.5 - to cr-row
  0.0 n 1.0 f- 1.0 matrix-range n 1 reshape 2.0 * n / 1.0 - to ci-col
  1.0 ones-col cr-row 0.0 n n 0-matrix dgemm-nn to c-real
  1.0 ci-col ones-row 0.0 n n 0-matrix dgemm-nn to c-imag
  n n 0-matrix to zr  n n 0-matrix to zi  n n 0-matrix to escaped ;

: step
  | zr2 zi2 |
  zr zr * to zr2
  zi zi * to zi2
  escaped  zr2 zi2 + 4.0 >  +! drop
  zi zr *! 2.0 *! c-imag +! drop
  zr2 zi2 -! c-real +! to zr ;

setup
now to t0
[: step :] max-iter times
escaped 0.0 eq sum to checksum
now t0 - to elapsed
"elapsed: " . elapsed . " s" . cr
"checksum: " . checksum . cr
bye
